-- MineSkillData: the rebirth skill tree.
--
-- GENERATED by skills/gen.js + skills/emit.js. Edit those, not this file.
--
-- The rule this table exists to enforce: every node is worth a BUDGET IN
-- MINESTATS POINTS, and its percentages are derived by dividing that budget by
-- each stat's weight. Two nodes that cost the same are worth the same, whatever
-- stat they happen to touch.
--
-- The hand-written table this replaces did not do that. It paid +2% blast
-- radius (weight 6.0, so 12 points) and +3% dirt break (weight 0.6, so 1.8
-- points) for the same 1 skill point -- a 6.7x difference in what you actually
-- got, and up to 10x inside a single row. All ten roads now come out at 1.00x
-- of each other.
--
-- Caps: MineStats caps are "from ALL sources stacked", so skills claim at most
-- SKILL_CAP_SHARE of each one and pets and runes keep the rest. Allocation is
-- cap-aware -- when a stat fills, the leftover spills across the rest of the
-- kit instead of silently evaporating.
